=== REASONING ===
Chosen approach:
  - XcodeGen spec (apps/apple/project.yml) checked in for reproducibility; generated .xcodeproj git-ignored.
    Rejected hand-maintained .pbxproj (merge-hostile) and Tuist (extra toolchain not in the version lock).
  - One shared SwiftUI source group (Sources/) built by both app targets (TeslaSync iOS, TeslaSync-macOS),
    adaptive at runtime (NavigationSplitView on macOS/iPad regular width, NavigationStack on iPhone compact).
    Rejected two separate source trees (violates ADR-002 "adaptive layout counts, not two codebases").
  - Shared.xcframework linked as a static framework dependency + a pre-build Run Script
    (Scripts/build-shared-xcframework.sh) that assembles it from the KMP core and stages it into Frameworks/.
    Rejected an SPM binaryTarget (the xcframework is produced by Gradle, not released as a versioned zip yet).
  - Theme.swift ships a system-driven theme (light/dark + Dynamic Type) with stable call sites
    (Theme.accent / Theme.background / .teslaSyncTheme()). P2 swaps in the generated Tokens.swift behind the
    same API → no view churn. This is real (not a stub): the shell honors appearance + Dynamic Type today.
  - Tests: SharedCoreReachableTests (XCTest reads Platform.name to prove the xcframework links) +
    AppLaunchUITests (XCUITest asserts foreground launch). Compiled into per-platform unit/UI test bundles.
  - Brand name rendered with Text(verbatim:) (brand names are not localized); no new string-catalog keys are
    invented here (the 4.4 MB translation.* catalog is Xcode-managed; real UI strings arrive with pages).

